The Players
The PE Firm: Ridgecrest Capital Partners
Ridgecrest Capital Partners is a mid-market private equity firm based in Chicago with $2.8
billion in assets under management across three active funds. They focus on acquiring and
growing fragmented service-industry businesses in the $15M-$75M revenue range, primarily
across commercial and residential services, healthcare services, and facility management. Their
current Fund III holds 14 portfolio companies.
Six months ago, Ridgecrest hired their first Technology Operating Partner, David Kaplan, a
former Deloitte senior manager who spent 8 years advising PE clients on digital transformation.
David was brought on with one mandate: figure out how to deploy AI across the portfolio to
improve margins before the next round of exits in 18-24 months. He has a $500K annual budget
for external AI vendors and the authority to deploy them into any portfolio company with CEO
buy-in.
David's problem: he knows the strategy side cold, but he does not have an implementation
team. He is one person. Ridgecrest does not have in-house developers. And the two consulting
firms he reached out to (a Big 4 and a mid-tier digital agency) quoted $300K-$500K per portfolio
company for a 6-month engagement, which would burn through his entire budget on a single
company.
The Portfolio Company: Greenline Mechanical Services
Greenline is a commercial HVAC and plumbing company headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona,
with 8 branch locations across Arizona, Nevada, and New Mexico. Ridgecrest acquired
Greenline 2 years ago as a platform company and has since completed 3 add-on acquisitions,
bringing the company from $22M to $48M in annual revenue and from 85 to 310 employees.
