phone.
How PDS Got the Deal
David Kaplan found PDS through a combination of three touchpoints over a 6-week period:
1. LinkedIn article: Ronald Parent published an article titled 'The $2M Phone Call
Problem: Why PE-Backed Service Companies Are Bleeding Revenue After Hours.'
David saw it because a former Deloitte colleague liked it. The article did not pitch PDS. It
laid out the math of missed calls in service businesses and what that means for EBITDA.
David bookmarked it.
2. Cold email: Two weeks later, a personalized email from PDS landed in David's inbox
through Smartlead. The email referenced Ridgecrest's service-industry portfolio and
asked a simple question: 'How are your portfolio companies handling the 25-30% of
inbound calls that go unanswered after hours?' No pitch. Just a question that hit a nerve
because David had just reviewed Greenline's call data and seen the exact same
problem.
3. Discovery call: David replied. Ronald got on a 30-minute call where he asked about
Greenline's tech stack, call volumes, and pain points. Ronald did not pitch. He listened.
Then he said: 'I can do a full AI readiness audit of Greenline in 3 weeks for $15K. You
will get a prioritized roadmap of every AI opportunity with projected EBITDA impact for
each one. If the numbers do not justify a full engagement, you have a document you can
use for any other vendor.' David said yes that day.
