PDS conducted a deep operational audit, not a technology audit. The goal was to understand
where the business loses money, misses revenue, or wastes labor hours, and then determine
which of those problems AI can solve.
• Call recording analysis: PDS requested 2 weeks of call recordings from RingCentral.
Talha built an automated pipeline that transcribed the recordings using Deepgram, then
classified each call by type (new customer, existing service request, sales inquiry, billing
question, vendor/spam). The findings were stark.
– 4,218 inbound calls in the sample period
– 1,181 (28%) abandoned, sent to voicemail, or handled by the answering service
– Of the 1,181 missed calls, an estimated 340 were new customer inquiries based
on caller ID matching and voicemail content
– At Greenline's average service ticket of $2,800, those 340 missed new-customer
calls represented roughly $952K in monthly revenue exposure
– The after-hours answering service was booking appointments on only 31% of
calls. The rest were told 'someone will call you back,' and 44% of those callbacks
never happened.
• CSR workflow observation: Ronald spent one full day at the Phoenix headquarters
sitting with the 3 customer service representatives. He documented every task they
performed across an 8-hour shift.
– 62% of their time was spent on scheduling, rescheduling, and confirming
appointments, work that could be automated
– 18% was spent on calls that could be handled by an AI agent (hours of operation,
service area questions, pricing estimates, appointment confirmations)
– Only 20% of their time was spent on tasks that genuinely required a human:
complex customer complaints, insurance coordination, multi-trade project
scheduling
• Sales pipeline review: PDS reviewed 90 days of Salesforce data from the 6-person
commercial sales team.
– The sales team was spending 40% of their time qualifying leads that came in
through the website and phone
– Of those leads, 55% were unqualified (residential callers, out-of-area, tire
kickers)
– Average time from lead to first meaningful sales contact: 4.2 days. Industry best
practice is under 1 hour.
• Dispatch and technician scheduling: Hilal reviewed the ServiceTitan configuration
and identified that dispatching was largely manual. Office managers at each branch
were spending 2-3 hours per day playing Tetris with technician schedules, often leaving
gaps or sending the wrong-skilled tech to a job.
