Sprint 1: AI Voice Agent (Weeks 1-4)
This was the highest-priority deployment because the ROI was the most immediate and the
most visible.
What PDS Built
A 24/7 AI voice agent deployed across all 8 Greenline locations, integrated with ServiceTitan
and RingCentral. The agent handles calls in three scenarios: after-hours (replacing the
answering service entirely), overflow during business hours (when all CSRs are on other calls),
and first-ring pickup (answering before a human CSR, handling simple requests, and warm-
transferring complex calls).
Voice and personality: The agent was configured with a female voice named 'Sarah' with a
warm, professional tone. The persona was calibrated to match the Southwest market, friendly
but efficient, no corporate stiffness. Sarah introduces herself as being with Greenline
Mechanical and never pretends to be human. If a caller asks, she identifies as an AI assistant.
Capabilities deployed:
• Books service appointments directly into ServiceTitan, checking technician availability in
real time
• Qualifies new customer inquiries: captures property type, square footage, system type,
urgency level, and preferred appointment windows
• Handles emergency triage: routes true emergencies (gas leak, flooding, no heat in
winter) to the on-call technician's cell phone with a warm handoff
• Answers FAQs: service areas, hours of operation, accepted payment methods, license
numbers, and insurance information
• Captures caller information for follow-up when a job cannot be booked immediately
• Sends automated text confirmations to callers after booking
Integration architecture:
• Vapi for voice AI orchestration with ElevenLabs for voice synthesis
