Voice agent optimization: Talha conducted a full review of every call that required human
escalation during weeks 1-8. The most common escalation reasons were: multi-system quotes
requiring on-site assessment (acceptable), customer anger over a previous visit (acceptable),
and requests for specific technicians by name (trainable). After retraining the agent to handle
technician-specific requests, the escalation rate dropped from 14% to 9%.
Review generation workflow: An automated post-service workflow that texts customers 2
hours after job completion with a satisfaction check. Happy customers (4-5 stars) are routed to
leave a Google review. Unhappy customers (1-3 stars) are routed to the Customer Success
Coordinator for immediate follow-up before they post a negative review publicly.
